content:
A seller whose Northloop Payments balance is below zero may settle it by authorising a card settlement against the card on file.

## Ledger state the card settlement waits on

A card settlement of a negative balance is not charged until every won chargeback case with a fee return due carries that fee-return entry on the payments ledger.

## Situation of use and capability

`pay_negative_balance_by_card_47b519ae` is the seller's authorisation of a card settlement of the negative balance on their own Northloop Payments account, charged to the payment card on file. One call books one successful card charge entry on the payments ledger for the amount given and raises the account's total balance by that amount; when the balance reaches zero or more, the account no longer shows a negative-balance date. The seller then sees the card charge in their payments history. The amount is taken exactly as given; nothing else on the account changes.

## How it is invoked

This is the customer's own tool: the support agent unlocks `pay_negative_balance_by_card_47b519ae` and hands it over, and the customer themselves runs it.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `payout_account_id` | the payments account reference number of the seller's own Northloop Payments account, as read out by the support agent from the payments account lookup | identifier |
| `amount` | the amount charged to the card on file, in USD, as stated by the support agent | a positive number with 2 decimal places (cents); booked exactly as given |

## Return

A text rendering of a dictionary describing the charge booked:

- `status` — the literal `card_charged` when the charge entry was booked;
- `payout_event_id` — reference of the new payments ledger entry;
- `charge_attempt` — the attempt number recorded for the charge (integer);
- `charge_outcome` — the literal `succeeded`;
- `amount` — the amount charged in USD with 2 decimal places;
- `balance` — the account's total balance in USD after the charge, 2 decimal places;
- `negative_since_date` — the date the balance went below zero, YYYY-MM-DD, or empty when it is zero or more;
- `event_date` — the date of the charge, YYYY-MM-DD.
